```ts
function displayName(name: string): string {
  return name.trim();
}
```
This evaluates the same expression once and returns the same string. Recommend the existing type check and focused examples for empty, whitespace-only and padded strings. No files changed or checks executed.

REF-42: retain the approved plan and propose step 2 only:
```ts
function uppercaseLabels(values: string[], locale: string): string[] {
  return values.map(value => value.toLocaleUpperCase(locale));
}

export function renderLabels(values: string[], locale: string): string[] {
  return uppercaseLabels(values, locale);
}
```
The helper takes the same arguments and preserves mapping order, locale conversion and error propagation. It remains local; no service or new error handling is introduced.

